#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Brief: Runs REIN on this machine: the LFT testbed, the REIN services (docker compose) and the console.
#   ./rein setup                  once: LFT next to REIN, the images, deployer/.env, the console's Python
#                                 packages, the NVIDIA Container Toolkit where there is an NVIDIA GPU, sudo
#                                 without a password for lft and docker, the console service, and the rein
#                                 command (/usr/local/bin/rein, a link to this file)
#   rein up [--topology T]        the testbed (only when none is running; T is a preset or a topology
#                                 file), the services and the console; ends with the console's address
#   rein down [--keep-testbed]    the console, the services and the testbed
#   rein status                   what is up
#   rein model [ID]               the models and which fit this machine's VRAM; with an ID, uses that one
# rein up also starts the model in use: the one chosen with rein model while it fits, else one whose
# server answers, else the largest of llm/models.yaml that fits (llm/compose.yml). When none fits,
# no model runs and the chat takes Nile.
# up and down show one line per task, as docker compose does: what it is doing while it runs, then a
# check and how long it took. What the commands print is kept and shown only when one fails.
#   rein logs SERVICE [-f]        deployer, supervisor, collector, profiler or console
# LFT_DIR (default: ../lft) is where LFT is, LFT_BRANCH the branch setup clones, LFT_BIN its lft.

